<title>JAPAN: Japan March lead imports down 10.7 pct yr/yr--MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan March lead imports down 10.7 pct yr/yr--MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's refined lead imports in March fell by 10.7 percent to 584 tonnes from 654 tonnes in the same month a year earlier, Finance Ministry data issued on Monday showed.</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		    Mar 97	    Feb 97	   Mar 96</p>
<p> Total		584	     1,153		654</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> China		225		 840		100</p>
<p> Peru		 221		 272		191</p>
<p>Cumulative imports in the first three months of 1997 were 3,748 tonnes, up from 3,177 tonnes in the same period a year earlier.</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
</text>
